15ba Phalc\u0101,\u00a0S\u0101\u1e25ga\u1e25, Kirtipur re the construction of\u00a0Manda\u1e25 Phalc\u0101 (NS 870)", "displayname_language": "en", "geometries": [{"geom": {"features": [{"geometry": {"coordinates": [85.2733513045817, 27.67881131725136], "type": "Point"}, "id": "75a577fc-199b-44f1-804d-36996777b8e9", "properties": {"nodeId": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007"}, "type": "Feature"}], "type": "FeatureCollection"}, "nodegroup_id": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007", "provisional": false, "tileid": "6cf28c65-08e8-401f-949d-2911a51f3aa3"}], "graph_id": "6215ee02-990d-11ea-9766-0242ac130005", "map_popup": [{"language": "en", "value": "<p>A stone inscription at&nbsp;S\u0101\u1e25ga\u1e25 Ga\u1e47e\u015ba Phalc\u0101,&nbsp;S\u0101\u1e25ga\u1e25, Kirtipur re the construction of&nbsp;Manda\u1e25 Phalc\u0101 (NS 870)</p>\n"}], "permissions": {"users_with_no_access": [], "users_without_delete_perm": [], "users_without_edit_perm": [], "users_without_read_perm": []}, "points": [{"nodegroup_id": "e871483e-c2b1-11ea-a1e8-0242ac120007", "point": {"lat": 27.67881131725136, "lon": 85.2733513045817}, "provisional": false}], "provisional_resource": "false", "resourceinstanceid": "0ae972fc-cb14-4a81-8219-c61b6dd0b490", "root_ontology_class": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E34_Inscription"}}, {"_id": "8c1dde36-7583-4c83-bd1e-c8ab7c5104e6", "_ignored": ["tiles.data.26ac8fa4-af81-11e9-a3d8-0242ac120005.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.66fd9c70-ce1b-11e9-b993-0242ac140002.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.d9f64830-9fc2-11e9-a638-0242ac140004.en.value.keyword", "tiles.data.d9f64efc-9fc2-11e9-a638-0242ac140004.en.value.keyword"], "_index": "danam_resources", "_score": 0.0, "_source": {"displaydescription": "<p>The pillars are located on both sides of the track, 15 minutes to the south-west of the village of&nbsp;Thokreya. Thokreya is found at a few kilometres south-west of Dullu.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>The four pillars are oriented to the south and display a variety of decorations. Pillar 001 is not decorated. Pillar 002 contains two circular motifs on the top, that probably represent the sun and the moon, or stars. Below it are traces of inscription. Pillar 003 is partly buried and tilted, but it remains possible to&nbsp;see a central st\u016bpa, surmounted by three circular motifs. Pillar 004 is broken in vertically broken in half. The top of the stele is occupied by a large flower motif with eight petals. Below is an eroded inscription where one can read &#39;\u015bake 1330&#39; (1408 CE).</p>\n\n<p>All of the pillars show traces of metal tools sharpening.</p>\n\n<p>Stone pillars were erected throughout the Karnali Basin from the 13th to the 17th century. They are installed to honor the memory of deceased persons, mostly warriors. In this case it is possible to situate the&nbsp;Thokreya stone memorial pillars between&nbsp;the 14th and the 15th century on the basis of their shape and the inscription of 1408 CE on pillar 004 (see&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/2247442/nhdp-bibliography/items/WWCCFK99/library\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Andolfatto 2019</strong></a>: p. 108).</p>\n", "displayname": "Thokreya stone memorial pillars || \u0925\u094b\u0915\u094d\u0930\u0947\u092f \u092a\u093e\u0937\u093e\u0923 \u0938\u094d\u092e\u0943\u0924\u093f\u0938\u094d\u0924\u092e\u094d\u092d\u0939\u0930\u0942 || DLK0240 ", "displayname_language": "en", "geometries": [], "graph_id": "f35cc1ca-9322-11e9-a5cc-0242ac120006", "map_popup": [{"language": "en", "value": "<p>The pillars are located on both sides of the track, 15 minutes to the south-west of the village of&nbsp;Thokreya. Thokreya is found at a few kilometres south-west of Dullu.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>The four pillars are oriented to the south and display a variety of decorations. Pillar 001 is not decorated. Pillar 002 contains two circular motifs on the top, that probably represent the sun and the moon, or stars. Below it are traces of inscription. Pillar 003 is partly buried and tilted, but it remains possible to&nbsp;see a central st\u016bpa, surmounted by three circular motifs. Pillar 004 is broken in vertically broken in half. The top of the stele is occupied by a large flower motif with eight petals. Below is an eroded inscription where one can read &#39;\u015bake 1330&#39; (1408 CE).</p>\n\n<p>All of the pillars show traces of metal tools sharpening.</p>\n\n<p>Stone pillars were erected throughout the Karnali Basin from the 13th to the 17th century. They are installed to honor the memory of deceased persons, mostly warriors. In this case it is possible to situate the&nbsp;Thokreya stone memorial pillars between&nbsp;the 14th and the 15th century on the basis of their shape and the inscription of 1408 CE on pillar 004 (see&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/2247442/nhdp-bibliography/items/WWCCFK99/library\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Andolfatto 2019</strong></a>: p. 108).</p>\n"}], "permissions": {"users_with_no_access": [], "users_without_delete_perm": [], "users_without_edit_perm": [], "users_without_read_perm": []}, "points": [], "provisional_resource": "false", "resourceinstanceid": "8c1dde36-7583-4c83-bd1e-c8ab7c5104e6", "root_ontology_class": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E71_Man-Made_Thing"}}, {"_id": "b7fa8fe1-cf3a-43de-94ab-8db58f68c418", "_ignored": ["tiles.data.2591e954-9a98-11ea-82af-0242ac130005.en.value.keyword"], "_index": "danam_resources", "_score": 0.0, "_source": {"displaydescription": "DLK0240_I_001", "displayname": "DLK0240_I_001 A stone inscription at\u00a0Thokreya stone memorial pillars,\u00a0Dullu,\u00a0Dailekh re the installation of pillar 004 (\u015aS 1330)", "displayname_language": "en", "geometries": [], "graph_id": "6215ee02-990d-11ea-9766-0242ac130005", "map_popup": [{"language": "en", "value": "<p>A stone inscription at&nbsp;Thokreya stone memorial pillars,&nbsp;Dullu,&nbsp;Dailekh re the installation of pillar 004 (\u015aS 1330)</p>\n"}], "permissions": {"users_with_no_access": [], "users_without_